I find Valks to be extremely beginner friendly class because:
Starting equipment (long sword is a good weapon in itself + starting
armor is not too shabby)
Starts with high strength and constitution, good HP growth/regen.
"Stupid" classes don't have to bother with spells in the beginning and
rely on brute strength.  Reading spellbooks is dangerous in the
beginning for casting classes anyways, and usually have to save the
books for later levels anyways.  So basically, while casters are
gimped in learning new spells, valks just keep doing what they do
best: hack & slash.
Mines usually hands out great metal armor for valks, much of which
casters have to pass on to preserve their casting abilities.
Fountains + Long Sword =3D Excalibur. Enough said.

